meta {
  name: Book Interview Slot
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/interviews/bookings
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{studentAccessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "application_id": "{{applicationId}}",
    "slot_id": "{{interviewSlotId}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 201) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    if (data.data && data.data.id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("interviewBookingId", data.data.id);
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Books an interview slot for the whole Application (not one specific
  course on it — an Application can carry several via "Add Course", and
  the student sits one shared interview covering all of them). One
  booking per Application, ever.

  409 ConflictError "This application is not currently at the interview
  stage" unless at least one non-withdrawn course's status is
  "assessment_completed" or already "interview_pending". 409 "You already
  have an interview booking for this application". 409 "You already have
  an active interview booking. Cancel it before booking another." — a
  student can only have ONE booking with status "booked" at a time, across
  every one of their Applications (not just this one) — cancel the
  existing booking first. 409 "This interview slot is fully booked"
  (capacity race lost).

  On success, every course that was at "assessment_completed" moves to
  "interview_pending" (idempotent no-op for ones already there, e.g. after
  a cancel + re-book). Courses not yet eligible are left untouched.

  For a "gmeet" slot: this is the point where the Google Meet link is
  actually created (not at slot creation time) — the response's
  `slot.meetingUrl`/`slot.meetingId` reflect the freshly-created link. If
  another student already booked this same slot earlier, the link already
  exists and is simply reused. Best-effort — stays `null` if Google Meet
  isn't configured or the call fails; booking still succeeds either way.
}
